Lever: shorter read batch windows under the old cost budget (steal report row 15, first try): reads wait 500 µs or
2 ms for company, still capped at an estimated 3 ms of Postgres per group. Base: 5a6ee6c. This file is the 2 ms
arm; the 500 µs arm differs only in the constant.

Measured (lv2 on t1, cap 3, 42,000 users, paired against HEAD in the same round, µs/request from monitor.sh):
  2 ms:   round 1 -38 (PG -34), round 2 -6 (PG -5; instructions -61k per request): -22 [-38, -6]
  500 µs: round 1 -80 (PG -67; HEAD ran first after the target's reboot); round 2 under the per-cgroup perf
          counters, left out
Superseded by the gather queue (825c365: one queue, a 5 ms clock, no cost budget, depth 1), which measured
-22.5 [-24, -21] with 2 pairs on t5 and is the shape sql-proto measured.

